          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most decks, buy the Wooster Bravo Stainer for an oil-based stain or the Wooster 4054 for a water-based one, put it on a short extension pole, and add a 3-inch brush with matching bristle for the railings. If the floor is large, add the Shur-Line pad to lay stain down faster and use the brush to work it in behind.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The Purdy XL Swan is worth its higher price only if you stain regularly and care about the finish on the railings. Whatever you buy, match the bristle to the stain, brush every board end to end, and never let a pad or roller be the last tool to touch the wood.
          </p>
